      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The industry standard is a clear line drawn at intent and impact, not just the content itself. Satire is protected speech when it targets ideas or policies, but it crosses into hate speech when it directly attacks protected groups based on immutable characteristics like race or religion. If the content's primary function is to incite violence or dehumanize a specific group, it is universally flagged as hate speech, regardless of the satirical framing.",
